{
  "id": "shenzhen-master-tournament",
  "name": "Shenzhen Master Tournament",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "The 2024 Shenzhen Master Tournament was held at the Shenzhen Convention and Exhibition Center on 21 and 22 December 2024. Buying one of a list of gift boxes at its shop came with a Lugia V with the tournament's logo, 1,500 in all, and another 500 went the same way at its pop-up in Shenzhen Talent Park from 19 December 2024 to 1 January 2025.\n\nThe 2025 Shenzhen Master Tournament was held at the same venue on 6 and 7 December 2025, with a team event for its open division. It was one of that year's four Master Tournaments (大师赛) in China, in Guangzhou, Hangzhou, Beijing and Shenzhen, whose prizes were Simplified Chinese holo Rare Candy cards stamped with the event and the player's result: a plain copy for a good record (the top 800 of the open division's preliminaries, seniors with four wins in their preliminaries and juniors with three wins in their breakthrough round), and Top 64, Top 8, 3rd Place, 2nd Place and Champion copies by final standing. The top finishers also got a Victory Symbol, the Simplified Chinese print of the trophy card of Japan's Champions League, stamped 3rd Place for those who finished third and fourth, 2nd Place or Champion.\n\nBuying designated card products came with a Roaring Moon ex with its logo: 3,500 at the tournament, 3,500 across the official Pokémon card gyms in Shenzhen and 1,000 at the official Pokémon store's pop-up for the event. Among the 2025 event's participation prizes was an event pack holding one of eight basic Energy cards with the tournament's logo, at random.",
    "sources": [
      {
